In convex quadrilateral $ABCD,$ $M$ and $N$ are the midpoints of $\overline{BC}$ and $\overline{AD}$, respectively.  Let $E$ be on $\overline{AC},$ and $F$ be on $\overline{BD},$ and let $G$ be the intersection of $\overline{EF}$ and $\overline{MN}.$  If $\overline{AC}$ and $\overline{BD}$ intersect at $O$ and $AE = 2BF,$ then find $\frac{EG}{GF}.$

[asy]
unitsize(0.3 cm);

pair A, B, C, D, E, F, G, M, N, O;
real x = 4;

B = (0,0);
C = (18,0);
D = (14,10);
A = (8,20);
M = (B + C)/2;
N = (A + D)/2;
E = interp(A,C,x/16);
F = interp(B,D,2*x/20);
G = extension(E,F,M,N);
O = intersectionpoint(A--C,B--D);

draw(A--B--C--D--cycle);
draw(E--F);
draw(M--N);

label("$A$", A, N);
label("$B$", B, SW);
label("$C$", C, SE);
label("$D$", D, NE);
label("$E$", E, NE);
label("$F$", F, NW);
label("$G$", G, S);
label("$M$", M, S);
label("$N$", N, N);
label("$O$", O, NW);
[/asy]

