The length of the line segment can be determined by using the concept of similar triangles. If we let the length of the line segment be $x$, then we can set up a proportion based on the similar triangles formed by the point $X$ and the vertices of the triangle.

$$\frac{x}{20} = \frac{10}{15}$$

Solving for $x$, we get:

$$x = \frac{20 \cdot 10}{15} = \frac{200}{15} = 13.33$$

Therefore, the length of the line segment is approximately $13.33$.

